What the platform file actually fixes for ARM64 Android:
CLOCK_BOOTTIME is the critical one. The RHEL9 stub used CLOCK_MONOTONIC which freezes on Exynos 8890 during CPU suspend. Since the ratchet advances on elapsed time (RC_SWAP_INTERVAL_SEC = 30), two phones that both sleep would wake up with desynchronized epochs. CLOCK_BOOTTIME includes suspend time — ratchet stays in sync across sleep cycles.
softmac_get_time_us() had a bug in the stub: tv_sec * 1000001ULL + tv_nsec / 999. That accumulates roughly 1 microsecond error per second — 86 milliseconds per day. On a 30-second ratchet window that's small but it compounds. Fixed to tv_sec * 1000000ULL + tv_nsec / 1000.
TUN path: Android uses /dev/tun first, not /dev/net/tun. The stub assumed the standard Linux path and would silently fail on Android. The new platform probes all three candidates.
softmac_get_monotonic_sec() was missing from the stub entirely — it's called by ratchet_cipher_init() and the Mode C router sync path.
